# a ListView is READONLY: `get` is its only element accessor, and `getMut`
# lives on the owning list. The refusal lands at EMIT rather than typecheck --
# a container mono is lenient about members it does not declare, so the
# undeclared call reaches the emitter as an unrouted callee.
Row: class {
    n: i64
}
main: function is {
    rows: (List Row)
    rows.append (Row n: 1)
    lv: rows.listView
    (lv.getMut i: 0)
}
